IMPORT prelude

-- ccc23-transfers.l4 -- sections 672.86 to 672.95 (Interprovincial Transfers; Enforcement of Orders and Regulations) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46; 672.95 (regulations) is machinery and has no rule here.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Form: see the header of ccc23-assessment.l4. No rule of this module names a time limit in days or months, so there is no date arithmetic and no regulative rule: the one timed duty (672.92(3), (4)) has no named actor ("the accused shall be taken before a justice"), and the module invents none; it is a decision function over hours.
-- Peace officer and justice are plain inputs: "peace officer" is defined by section 2 (an "includes" list) and is asked as a fact; "justice" is a person the facts name.

§ `Section 672.86 -- Interprovincial transfers`

-- 672.86(1): an accused who is detained in custody or directed to attend at a hospital pursuant to a disposition made by a court or Review Board under paragraph 672.54(c) or a court under section 672.58 may be transferred to any other place in Canada where
-- (a) the Review Board of the province where the accused is detained or directed to attend recommends a transfer for the purpose of the reintegration of the accused into society or the recovery, treatment or custody of the accused; and
-- (b) the Attorney General of the province to which the accused is being transferred, or an officer authorized by that Attorney General, and the Attorney General of the province from which the accused is being transferred, or an officer authorized by that Attorney General, give their consent.
-- Two layers of limit: the description of the accused (a scope limit: NOTHING outside it) and the "where" gate (a "where" condition: JUST FALSE when it fails, by the ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); listed for a lawyer as F-GRANT-WHERE).
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
