§ `Sections 672.9 to 672.95 -- Enforcement of orders and regulations`

-- 672.9: any warrant or process issued in relation to an assessment order or disposition made in respect of an accused may be executed or served in any place in Canada outside the province where the order or disposition was made as if it had been issued in that province.
-- src:14033 | Execution of warrant anywhere in Canada
-- src:14034 | 672.9 Any warrant or process issued in relation to an assessment order or disposition made in respect of an accused may be executed or served in any place in Canada outside the province where the order or disposition was made as if it had been issued in that province.
@ref s 672.9 (src:14033-14034)
GIVEN `it is a warrant or process issued in relation to an assessment order or disposition made in respect of an accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is in Canada outside the province where the order or disposition was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.9 the warrant or process may be executed or served in the place as if it had been issued in that province` MEANS
    IF `it is a warrant or process issued in relation to an assessment order or disposition made in respect of an accused` AND `the place is in Canada outside the province where the order or disposition was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any warrant or process issued in relation to an assessment order or disposition made in respect of an accused may be executed or served in any place in Canada outside the province where the order or disposition was made"

-- 672.91: a peace officer may arrest an accused without a warrant at any place in Canada if the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has contravened or wilfully failed to comply with the assessment order or disposition or any condition of it, or is about to do so.
-- "Peace officer" is defined by section 2 (an "includes" list), so it is asked as a fact whose answer may itself be not covered.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
-- src:14035 | Arrest without warrant for contravention of disposition
-- src:14036 | 672.91 A peace officer may arrest an accused without a warrant at any place in Canada if the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has contravened or wilfully failed to comply with the assessment order or disposition or any condition of it, or is about to do so.
@ref s 672.91 (src:14035-14036)
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has contravened the assessment order or disposition or any condition of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has wilfully failed to comply with the assessment order or disposition or any condition of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused is about to contravene or wilfully fail to comply with the assessment order or disposition or any condition of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.91 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant` MEANS
    IF `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the place is in Canada` AND (`the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has contravened the assessment order or disposition or any condition of it` OR `the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has wilfully failed to comply with the assessment order or disposition or any condition of it` OR `the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused is about to contravene or wilfully fail to comply with the assessment order or disposition or any condition of it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has contravened or wilfully failed to comply with the assessment order or disposition or any condition of it, or is about to do so"

-- 672.92(1): if a peace officer arrests an accused under section 672.91 who is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or an assessment order, the peace officer, as soon as practicable, may release the accused from custody and
-- (a) issue a summons or appearance notice compelling the accused's appearance before a justice; and (b) deliver the accused to the place specified in the disposition or assessment order.
-- The conduct asked about is the whole package, as the text states it: release, and (a) a summons or appearance notice, and (b) delivery to the place specified.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
-- src:14037 | Release or delivery of accused subject to paragraph 672.54(b) disposition order
-- src:14038 | 672.92 (1) If a peace officer arrests an accused under section 672.91 who is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or an assessment order, the peace officer, as soon as practicable, may release the accused from custody and
-- src:14039 | (a) issue a summons or appearance notice compelling the accused’s appearance before a justice; and
-- src:14040 | (b) deliver the accused to the place specified in the disposition or assessment order.
@ref s 672.92; s 672.92(1); s 672.92(1)(a); s 672.92(1)(b) (src:14037-14040)
GIVEN `a peace officer arrests the accused under section 672.91` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or an assessment order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer acts as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer issues a summons or appearance notice compelling the accused’s appearance before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the peace officer delivers the accused to the place specified in the disposition or assessment order` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.92(1) the peace officer may release the accused from custody, issue a summons or appearance notice and deliver the accused to the place specified` MEANS
    IF `a peace officer arrests the accused under section 672.91` AND `the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or an assessment order` AND `the peace officer acts as soon as practicable` AND `the peace officer issues a summons or appearance notice compelling the accused’s appearance before a justice` AND `the peace officer delivers the accused to the place specified in the disposition or assessment order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a peace officer arrests an accused under section 672.91 who is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or an assessment order, the peace officer, as soon as practicable, may release the accused from custody and"

-- 672.92(2): a peace officer shall not release an accused under subsection (1) if the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds,
-- (a) that it is necessary in the public interest that the accused be detained in custody having regard to all the circumstances, including the need to (i) establish the identity of the accused, (ii) establish the terms and conditions of a disposition made under section 672.54 or of an assessment order, (iii) prevent the commission of an offence, or (iv) prevent the accused from contravening or failing to comply with the disposition or assessment order;
-- (b) that the accused is subject to a disposition or an assessment order of a court, or Review Board, of another province; or (c) that, if the accused is released from custody, the accused will fail to attend, as required, before a justice.
-- The bar is named as a bar: JUST TRUE = subsection (1) does not allow the release. The flat "shall not" is limited by an "if", so outside the three beliefs the answer is NOTHING (F-BAR-IF).
-- fork: F-BAR-IF
-- src:14041 | No release
-- src:14042 | (2) A peace officer shall not release an accused under subsection (1) if the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds,
-- src:14043 | (a) that it is necessary in the public interest that the accused be detained in custody having regard to all the circumstances, including the need to
-- src:14044 | (i) establish the identity of the accused,
-- src:14045 | (ii) establish the terms and conditions of a disposition made under section 672.54 or of an assessment order,
-- src:14046 | (iii) prevent the commission of an offence, or
-- src:14047 | (iv) prevent the accused from contravening or failing to comply with the disposition or assessment order;
-- src:14048 | (b) that the accused is subject to a disposition or an assessment order of a court, or Review Board, of another province; or
-- src:14049 | (c) that, if the accused is released from custody, the accused will fail to attend, as required, before a justice.
@ref s 672.92(2); s 672.92(2)(a); s 672.92(2)(b); s 672.92(2)(c) (src:14041-14049)
GIVEN `a peace officer arrests the accused under section 672.91` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or an assessment order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that it is necessary in the public interest that the accused be detained in custody having regard to all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that the accused is subject to a disposition or an assessment order of a court, or Review Board, of another province` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that, if the accused is released from custody, the accused will fail to attend, as required, before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.92(2) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused under subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a peace officer arrests the accused under section 672.91` AND `the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or an assessment order`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an accused under subsection (1)"
        IF `the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that it is necessary in the public interest that the accused be detained in custody having regard to all the circumstances` OR `the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that the accused is subject to a disposition or an assessment order of a court, or Review Board, of another province` OR `the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that, if the accused is released from custody, the accused will fail to attend, as required, before a justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not release an accused under subsection (1) if the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds,"

-- 672.92(2)(a)(i)-(iv): the circumstances the officer has regard to "including the need to" do the four things listed. The word "including" leaves the list open: a need outside the four is not covered.
-- src:14044 | (i) establish the identity of the accused,
-- src:14045 | (ii) establish the terms and conditions of a disposition made under section 672.54 or of an assessment order,
-- src:14046 | (iii) prevent the commission of an offence, or
-- src:14047 | (iv) prevent the accused from contravening or failing to comply with the disposition or assessment order;
@ref s 672.92(2)(a)(i); s 672.92(2)(a)(ii); s 672.92(2)(a)(iii); s 672.92(2)(a)(iv) (src:14044-14047)
DECLARE `s 672.92(2)(a) need` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.92(2)(a)(i) establish the identity of the accused`
    `s 672.92(2)(a)(ii) establish the terms and conditions of a disposition made under section 672.54 or of an assessment order`
    `s 672.92(2)(a)(iii) prevent the commission of an offence`
    `s 672.92(2)(a)(iv) prevent the accused from contravening or failing to comply with the disposition or assessment order`
    `s 672.92(2)(a) another need`

-- src:14043 | (a) that it is necessary in the public interest that the accused be detained in custody having regard to all the circumstances, including the need to
-- src:14044 | (i) establish the identity of the accused,
-- src:14045 | (ii) establish the terms and conditions of a disposition made under section 672.54 or of an assessment order,
-- src:14046 | (iii) prevent the commission of an offence, or
-- src:14047 | (iv) prevent the accused from contravening or failing to comply with the disposition or assessment order;
@ref s 672.92(2)(a) (src:14043-14047)
GIVEN `the need` IS A `s 672.92(2)(a) need`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.92(2)(a) the need is one of those that the circumstances include` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the need`
        WHEN `s 672.92(2)(a)(i) establish the identity of the accused` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 672.92(2)(a)(ii) establish the terms and conditions of a disposition made under section 672.54 or of an assessment order` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 672.92(2)(a)(iii) prevent the commission of an offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 672.92(2)(a)(iv) prevent the accused from contravening or failing to comply with the disposition or assessment order` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 672.92(2)(a) another need` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including the need to"

-- 672.92(3): if a peace officer does not release the accused, the accused shall be taken before a justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the accused is arrested, without unreasonable delay and in any event within twenty-four hours after the arrest.
-- The text names no one who takes the accused, so no actor is invented: the duty is a decision function, and its time limit another, over the hours after the arrest.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
